# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TradeReply AI — example environment file
#
# TEMPLATE ONLY. This file is tracked by git (.gitignore ignores ".env*" but
# re-includes "!.env.example"), so it must never hold a real API key.
#
# Copy it, then paste your own values:
#   copy .env.example .env.local      (Windows)
#   cp   .env.example .env.local      (macOS / Linux)
#
# server.ts loads .env.local first and then .env. dotenv never overwrites a key
# that is already set, so .env.local always wins. If a value you set here looks
# ignored, look for a stale .env.local shadowing it.
#
# In AI Studio this key is injected at runtime from the Secrets panel
# (Settings → Secrets); locally you must set it yourself.
#
# IMPORTANT: every AI endpoint calls the real Gemini API. If this key is absent
# the endpoints return HTTP 503 AI_ENGINE_NOT_CONFIGURED — they never return
# simulated, canned or placeholder AI output. See README → "Live engine".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Required --------------------------------------------------------------

# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required. Create one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Deliberately left EMPTY in this template: the server only checks that the
# value is non-empty, so a leftover placeholder such as "your_api_key_here"
# counts as configured and makes every AI call fail upstream
# (401/403 → 500) instead of reporting the clear 503
# AI_ENGINE_NOT_CONFIGURED. With an empty value the server logs
# "GEMINI_API_KEY is NOT set" at startup and GET /api/health reports "offline".
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Optional --------------------------------------------------------------

# GEMINI_MODEL: Optional. Overrides the model used by every AI endpoint.
# Defaults to gemini-3.8-flash (Google's current stable Flash model).
# Commented out on purpose so server.ts stays the single source of truth for
# the default; uncomment only to pin a different model. Prefer a stable model
# id over a moving alias ("gemini-3.8-flash", not "gemini-flash-latest"). An
# unsupported id makes GET /api/health return 502 and the other AI endpoints
# return 500.
# Models:        https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models
# Deprecations:  https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/deprecations
#GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash

# GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODELS: Optional. Ordered, comma-separated list of further REAL
# models tried when the primary is temporarily unavailable upstream (Google
# returns 503 UNAVAILABLE "experiencing high demand" under load). server.ts
# retries the primary with backoff, then walks this list. Whichever model actually
# served a request is reported back as `engine` in every response, so a fallback is
# never silent — and if all models fail, the endpoint returns an error rather than
# inventing content. Set it empty to disable fallbacks entirely.
#
# Defaults are models verified responding live; gemini-2.5-flash is deliberately
# NOT included because it now returns 404 "no longer available to new users".
#GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODELS=gemini-3.6-flash,gemini-3.5-flash,gemini-3.5-flash-lite,gemini-3.1-flash-lite

# GEMINI_TIMEOUT_MS: Optional. Hard ceiling per model attempt, in milliseconds
# (default 25000 — matches the default in server.ts). Bounds one attempt so a hung
# socket or a congested model cannot stall the whole chain. The abort is treated as
# transient, so the chain moves on to the next model rather than failing outright.
#GEMINI_TIMEOUT_MS=25000

# GEMINI_TOTAL_BUDGET_MS: Optional. Overall budget for the entire retry + fallback
# chain, in milliseconds (default 60000). Each attempt is bounded by the smaller of
# GEMINI_TIMEOUT_MS and the remaining budget, so total latency stays predictable no
# matter how many models are listed above. Raise it if you would rather keep trying
# under heavy upstream load than return a fast, honest transient error.
#GEMINI_TOTAL_BUDGET_MS=60000

# --- Optional local Ollama provider -----------------------------------------

# OLLAMA_MODEL: Optional. Enables a SECOND REAL provider backed by a local
# Ollama daemon — real model, no API key, no per-token cost. It is never a mock.
#
#   - With GEMINI_API_KEY set, Ollama is appended as the LAST entry of the retry
#     chain, so a Google outage or quota stop no longer means "no replies".
#   - With no GEMINI_API_KEY, the local model is promoted to PRIMARY and the app
#     serves real replies with no hosted key at all.
#
# Start the daemon and pull the model first:
#   ollama serve
#   ollama pull llama3.2
# At boot the server calls GET /api/tags and DISABLES the Ollama targets if the
# daemon is unreachable or the model has not been pulled, logging exactly which.
# Unreachable Ollama never fails a request: it is simply skipped.
#OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2

# OLLAMA_FALLBACK_MODELS: Optional. Comma-separated further local models, tried
# in order when the previous one fails. Names may be written bare ("qwen2.5") or
# prefixed ("ollama:qwen2.5") — a bare name here is always treated as Ollama, so
# it can never be silently sent to Gemini.
#OLLAMA_FALLBACK_MODELS=qwen2.5,llama3.1

# OLLAMA_BASE_URL: Optional. Daemon address (default http://127.0.0.1:11434).
# Set this when Ollama runs on another host or behind a reverse proxy. A value
# that is not a valid http(s) URL disables Ollama and is reported at startup.
#OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS: Optional. Per-attempt ceiling for a local model, in ms
# (default 45000). Local CPU inference is slower than a hosted flash model, so
# this is deliberately higher than GEMINI_TIMEOUT_MS; the per-attempt bound used
# is the larger of the two whenever Ollama is enabled.
#OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS=45000

# --- API hardening (optional, recommended for any public deployment) --------

# TRADEREPLY_API_TOKEN: Optional. When set, every AI route requires the matching
# value in an "x-tradereply-token" header (or "Authorization: Bearer <token>") and
# requests without it get 401 UNAUTHORIZED. The exported extension's options page has
# a field for the same value. This is a speed bump against scanners, NOT user
# authentication: a value shipped to a browser bundle or an extension is not a
# secret. Real per-user auth plus quotas is the fix for a public deployment.
#TRADEREPLY_API_TOKEN=

# RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE: Optional. Fixed-window per-IP limit per AI route (default
# 20). Exceeding it returns 429 with a Retry-After header. The limiter lives in
# process memory, so with N server instances the effective limit is N x this value.
#RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=20

# HEALTH_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE: Optional. Separate limit for GET /api/health
# (default 10). The probe is deliberately not token-protected — the app footer uses
# it as a liveness indicator — but it does spend one small model call per hit.
#HEALTH_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=10

# MAX_REQUEST_BYTES: Optional. Express JSON body ceiling (default 64kb, was 10mb).
# Anything larger is rejected with 413 PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE before reaching the model.
#MAX_REQUEST_BYTES=64kb

# VITE_TRADEREPLY_API_TOKEN: Optional and build-time only — Vite inlines it into the
# client bundle, so it is public the moment it is built. Set it to the same value as
# TRADEREPLY_API_TOKEN only so the web hub keeps working when a token is enforced.
#VITE_TRADEREPLY_API_TOKEN=

# PORT: Optional. Port for the local API + app server. Defaults to 3000.
# Any non-numeric value silently falls back to the default.
#PORT=3000

# NODE_ENV: Optional. Set to "production" to serve the built bundle from dist/
# (run `npm run build` first). Any other value, including unset, loads the Vite
# dev middleware instead.
#NODE_ENV=production

# DISABLE_HMR: Optional, development only. Set to "true" to turn off Vite HMR
# and file watching. Used by the AI Studio agent environment to avoid flicker.
#DISABLE_HMR=true

# APP_URL: Optional. AI Studio injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run
# service URL. Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API
# endpoints. No source file reads it today, so leave it commented out here —
# and never set it to a literal placeholder like "MY_APP_URL", which would be
# treated as a real URL if a feature ever starts reading it.
#APP_URL=https://your-cloud-run-service-url
